==Strategy==
This stage might only be veteran difficulty, but don't let that fool you. The boss, Awakened EVA Unit-13, attacks often, allowing it to perma-weaken your cats, as well as perma-freezing them if a cat stays in its standing range without being knocked back. It also knocks back cats and is immune to waves, allowing it to push extremely easily. On top of this, it has Omni-strike hitting all the way up to 1200 range, even being able to hit even [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]! However, it has one weakness: its standing range is a low 200, which can be exploited by high-DPS Attackers from a distance, however, this makes recovering ground after an attack almost impossible unless your meatshields can survive the 15,000 damage hit AND are immune to Knockback or Freeze.

The [[You Will Find Happiness (Combo)|You Will Find Happiness]] combo ([[Kaworu & Cat (Special Cat)|Kaworu]] and [[Shinji & Cat (Rare Cat)|Shinji]]) is extremely helpful, especially when using more EVA Angel Killers.

[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can be of great help if aided by [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs cat]] or something else to clear the peons.

[[Mari Illustrious (Super Rare Cat)|Mari Illustrious]] is also highly useful for this stage, due to her immunity to freeze.

